2. Fundamental Rules to Note for Revision
A. Pointer Movement Rule
 * The Golden Rule: In any Two-Pointer technique (opposite-ends or same-direction), always ensure pointers move toward their termination condition (left++, right--). Missing pointer updates lead to infinite loops.
 * Condition Choice (left < right vs left <= right):
   * When reversing/swapping, use left < right. When left == right (the middle element in an odd-length array), swapping an element with itself is unnecessary work.
B. Crucial Edge Cases for Any Array Problem
Always test these scenarios before declaring your solution complete:
 * Null Check: if (arr == null) return;
 * Empty Array: arr.length == 0
